@startuml Collaboration to History — Session Cleanup
!theme plain
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Collaboration → History Service — Session End & Cleanup

actor "User A" as UA
actor "User B" as UB
participant "Collab Service\n(Socket.IO)" as Collab
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "History Service" as HS
database "Redis\n(Sessions)" as Redis
database "Firestore\n(session_history)" as FS

== Active Session ==

UA <-> Collab: Yjs editor + chat (WebSocket)
UB <-> Collab: Yjs editor + chat (WebSocket)

note over Collab, Redis
  During the session, every code edit triggers:
  - RPUSH session:{id}:ydoc (Yjs binary update)
  - SET session:{id}:finalCode (plaintext snapshot)
  Chat messages are stored in session:{id}:chat
end note

== User A Disconnects ==

UA ->x Collab: WebSocket disconnect
Collab -> Collab: Remove User A from\nconnectedEditors set
Collab -> UB: emit 'user-left'\n{userId, message}

note over Collab: connectedEditors.size == 1\nNo cleanup timer started

== User B Disconnects ==

UB ->x Collab: WebSocket disconnect
Collab -> Collab: Remove User B from\nconnectedEditors set
Collab -> Collab: connectedEditors.size == 0\nStart 30-second cleanup timer

note over Collab: If either user reconnects\nwithin 30s, timer is cancelled

== 30 Seconds Later (No Reconnect) ==

Collab -> GW: POST /internal/collab/session-ended/{sessionId}
activate GW

GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:meta
Redis --> GW: {user1_id, user2_id,\nquestionId, topic, difficulty, startedAt}

GW -> Redis: GET session:{id}:finalCode
Redis --> GW: "function hello() { ... }"

GW -> GW: Build history payload\n{...meta, finalCode, endedAt}

GW -> HS: POST /history
activate HS
HS -> FS: Set document(sessionId)\nin session_history collection
FS --> HS: OK
HS --> GW: 201 Created
deactivate HS

GW -> Redis: DELETE session:{id}:meta\nsession:{id}:finalCode\nsession:{id}:ydoc\nsession:{id}:chat
Redis --> GW: OK

GW --> Collab: 200 {detail: "Session ended\nand history saved"}
deactivate GW

Collab -> Collab: sessions.delete(sessionId)\n(remove from in-memory Map)

@enduml
